Del, how's it going?

00:51:54.040 --> 00:51:55.920
All right, my son. Sit down and have a shot with Papa Dump.

00:51:56.020 --> 00:51:57.240
No, listen, I can't get involved.

00:51:57.400 --> 00:51:59.100
I'm getting a missus a takeaway and I want to get home tonight.

00:51:59.220 --> 00:51:59.980
Oh, you...

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:04.780
got time for a drink. Go on, sit down. Oh, cheers. I'm glad I bumped into you. I want you to do me a

00:52:04.780 --> 00:52:10.930
favour. What's that? Oh, sit down. You know those broken lawnmower engines that dozy twonk Rodney got

00:52:10.930 --> 00:52:15.670
himself lumbered with? Yeah, what about them? I want you to buy them off him. You want me to do what?

00:52:16.380 --> 00:52:20.780
Do me a favour, Del. Alfie Flowers offered me them engines a month ago. I don't want nothing to do

00:52:20.780 --> 00:52:26.510
with them. It's all right. It's all right. Listen, you don't have to spend any money. I'll give you the money.

00:52:28.460 --> 00:52:29.100
Yeah, I'll see that. Look.

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:32.000
200 quid, I want you to offer him that.

00:52:32.640 --> 00:52:36.020
200? Here, they're only worth about a score of scrap value.

00:52:37.030 --> 00:52:39.450
I know, but I want him to think he's made a good profit.

00:52:39.570 --> 00:52:41.490
Look, he's had a bad week, he's been tucked up,

00:52:41.610 --> 00:52:43.310
something chronic by that best mate of his,

00:52:43.350 --> 00:52:44.010
and now he's brassy.

00:52:44.170 --> 00:52:45.230
Why don't you just give him the money?

00:52:45.870 --> 00:52:47.230
Well, because he seemed like charity, wouldn't he?

00:52:49.940 --> 00:52:50.200
Yeah.

00:52:51.030 --> 00:52:52.190
And he'd be too proud to accept it?

00:52:52.250 --> 00:52:53.350
No, he'd snap it up like a shot.

00:52:55.460 --> 00:52:58.660
I want him to think that he's been successful.

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:01.780
I want him to believe that he's proved me wrong.

00:53:02.720 --> 00:53:04.040
It's important, Towson.

00:53:06.240 --> 00:53:06.840
All right, then, Dale.

00:53:07.210 --> 00:53:08.820
If that's what you want, he'll repel.

00:53:11.480 --> 00:53:13.020
Don't let him know that I...

00:53:14.680 --> 00:53:18.300
You say to him that you've got this contact in the GLC Parks Department

00:53:18.300 --> 00:53:21.420
and they can't get enough lawnmower engines, something like that.

00:53:21.660 --> 00:53:24.420
You see, the thing is, I'm not going to lose out on the deal.

00:53:25.560 --> 00:53:28.920
Because come this time tomorrow, Rodney will want to be my partner again

00:53:28.920 --> 00:53:29.960
and I will...

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:36.430
get my money back that's it hey wait a minute what am i going to do with all these engines

00:53:36.430 --> 00:53:41.150
why don't i dump them somewhere oh no no i couldn't do that del i mean i got nick for fly

00:53:41.150 --> 00:53:44.790
dumping a couple of months ago i mean they're going to chuck the book at me this time i'll

00:53:44.790 --> 00:53:48.750
tell you what you do take them back to alfie flowers and tell him that he can have them for

00:53:48.750 --> 00:53:59.900
nothing yeah all right here hang about what's in it for me give you 50.

00:54:00.410 --> 00:54:11.380
Oh, yeah, 20. That'd do. Thank you. Anything for a mate? I wouldn't pay that bill if I were you.

00:54:12.870 --> 00:54:13.870
Thank you, darling. Good night.

00:54:20.850 --> 00:54:22.700
All right, brothers. Yeah.

00:54:24.560 --> 00:54:29.980
Hey, look, I've had a right blinding day. Look at that, though. Yeah, I must tell you. There's a...

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:31.800
Really silly bloke down the market today.

00:54:31.980 --> 00:54:33.340
Think he must have come from a funny farm.

00:54:33.640 --> 00:54:34.560
It was really silly.

00:54:35.020 --> 00:54:36.000
I said to him, I said,

00:54:36.200 --> 00:54:39.040
Here, do you want to buy some broken lawnmower engines?

00:54:39.320 --> 00:54:40.040
And he said to me,

00:54:40.200 --> 00:54:41.080
I ain't that silly.

00:54:42.140 --> 00:54:44.960
For your information, Derek,

00:54:45.140 --> 00:54:47.500
this morning I successfully negotiated

00:54:47.500 --> 00:54:50.340
the sale of them engines to young Towson.

00:54:51.060 --> 00:54:52.020
You're kidding me.

00:54:52.460 --> 00:54:52.680
No.

00:54:53.040 --> 00:54:54.800
On my life, he's bought the lot.

00:54:55.100 --> 00:54:57.800
He's got a contact in the Parks Department at the GLC.

00:54:58.200 --> 00:54:59.910
Cool. Well, that's a stroke of luck then, isn't it?

00:55:00.250 --> 00:55:03.920
No, no, it's not luck, Del. That is good business sense.

00:55:04.550 --> 00:55:07.670
I knew all the time if I held on long enough, I'd get my price.

00:55:08.340 --> 00:55:10.320
Well, I must say I admire your courage, Rudders.

00:55:10.520 --> 00:55:13.040
Well, he who dares wins.

00:55:15.520 --> 00:55:16.220
Yeah, that's right.

00:55:18.340 --> 00:55:21.760
So, well, that Mickey Pierce, he's going to be pleased when he comes back off holiday, isn't he, eh?

00:55:21.840 --> 00:55:23.800
Now, don't you talk to me about that Mickey Pierce.

00:55:24.290 --> 00:55:25.990
I've liquidated our partnership.

00:55:26.680 --> 00:55:26.900
Oh.

00:55:28.050 --> 00:55:29.050
So, what are you going to do, then?

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:31.560
I mean, you're still carrying on on your own, right?

00:55:33.620 --> 00:55:38.260
Well, I was thinking, oh, you know.

00:55:40.530 --> 00:55:42.650
Go back as we was, eh? You and me.

00:55:43.470 --> 00:55:45.570
Yeah, you and me do, eh?

00:55:45.930 --> 00:55:48.610
And now I've got experience in buying and selling myself.

00:55:49.710 --> 00:55:51.330
Yeah, that could be invaluable, Rodders.

00:55:53.280 --> 00:55:54.960
OK, then, come on, let's pool our resources.

00:55:55.460 --> 00:55:56.200
There we go.

00:55:57.040 --> 00:55:59.830
Now then, how much did you get for them Normo engines?

00:56:01.180 --> 00:56:01.500
£165.

00:56:02.100 --> 00:56:08.680
All you got for them, Rodney?

00:56:09.220 --> 00:56:12.780
Well, it's not bad, Del, because they're only worth, what, a score, scrap value.

00:56:13.550 --> 00:56:13.770
Hmm.

00:56:14.340 --> 00:56:16.220
Certainly have learnt a lot, haven't you, Rodders?

00:56:17.340 --> 00:56:18.460
OK, let's see the colour of your money.

00:56:18.880 --> 00:56:19.580
Well, I ain't got it.

00:56:20.580 --> 00:56:22.140
What do you mean? That Towser didn't pay you?

00:56:22.860 --> 00:56:24.940
Oh, yeah, he paid me, but I've invested the money.

00:56:25.540 --> 00:56:25.840
Did you what?

00:56:26.840 --> 00:56:29.980
I went down to Alfie Flowers Yard, got us another load of lawnmower engines.

00:56:41.960 --> 00:56:43.900
Joking, tell me that you're joking.

00:56:44.160 --> 00:56:46.580
No, he tells this bloke at the GLC,

00:56:46.780 --> 00:56:48.340
well, he can't get enough of them engines.

00:56:49.310 --> 00:56:51.590
Oh, you can tell me, I was dead lucky down at Alfie's.

00:56:51.710 --> 00:56:53.870
He'd had another load delivered this morning.

00:56:54.810 --> 00:56:57.940
I don't worry, though, because they're exactly the same as the others.

00:57:02.430 --> 00:57:04.030
You can bet your life they're the same.

00:57:06.280 --> 00:57:10.120
What a 42-carat plonker you really are!

00:57:10.340 --> 00:57:14.840
Come on, Del, don't you think it's time you showed a bit of faith in me?

00:57:15.990 --> 00:57:19.050
Yes, anything you say, Rodney, anything you say.

00:57:19.310 --> 00:57:19.750
Good.

00:57:21.240 --> 00:57:24.150
Oi, Del, I was wondering, now that we're partners again,

00:57:24.250 --> 00:57:26.240
do you think you could help me out, eh?

00:57:26.860 --> 00:57:29.410
Because I ain't had a pint all week.

00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:34.220
All I've had to eat is Grandad's cooking, and look, the soul's coming off me best Gucci.

00:57:34.840 --> 00:57:34.980
Look.

00:57:36.680 --> 00:57:38.240
Yeah, I'll help you out, Rodders.

00:57:40.120 --> 00:57:43.000
Put that round your Gucci, it'll stop the soul coming off.

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:02.660
fancy treksuits from a mushing shepherd's bush

00:58:02.750 --> 00:58:04.010
tax

00:58:07.030 --> 00:58:07.930
VAT

00:58:07.930 --> 00:58:09.710
no money back

00:58:10.090 --> 00:58:11.010
guarantee

00:58:11.010 --> 00:58:16.190
black hole at your prices

00:58:16.190 --> 00:58:28.600
and a straw same

00:58:30.320 --> 00:58:31.080
Lookie Street.

00:59:00.030 --> 00:59:05.900
I swear it's a mystery

00:59:06.400 --> 00:59:12.470
It's like the changing of seasons and driving

00:59:33.070 --> 00:59:35.600
Oh, oh, slow me.

00:59:36.710 --> 00:59:37.890
Here we are.

00:59:42.440 --> 00:59:43.900
Guess where we're going at a weekend.

00:59:44.620 --> 00:59:45.760
Give us a clue.

00:59:46.270 --> 00:59:48.190
All right, Robbie, if you insist.

00:59:48.530 --> 00:59:48.930
There you are.

00:59:49.050 --> 00:59:51.450
Ow, you dirty pig!

00:59:51.750 --> 00:59:52.450
Get it away!

00:59:53.080 --> 00:59:54.080
How's that rice going down?

00:59:54.240 --> 00:59:54.420
All right.

00:59:54.960 --> 00:59:58.220
Oh, where are we going then, Del?

00:59:58.770 --> 00:59:59.850
We're going skiing.

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:02.060
Where do you think we're going, you silly old...

01:00:02.060 --> 01:00:03.100
We're going fishing, aren't we?

01:00:03.240 --> 01:00:04.960
Well, I know that. I mean, where?

01:00:05.520 --> 01:00:07.700
Oh, see what you mean? We're going to a place called Tregower.

01:00:08.040 --> 01:00:08.540
Where's that?

01:00:08.700 --> 01:00:09.220
It's at Cornwall.

01:00:10.040 --> 01:00:12.560
Cornwall? Why are we going all the way down there?

01:00:12.820 --> 01:00:14.540
Cos that's where Boyce's weekend cottage is.

01:00:14.660 --> 01:00:16.280
I had dinner with him last night at Mario's,

01:00:16.320 --> 01:00:18.740
and he happened to mention he'd got his weekend cottage and it was free,

01:00:18.840 --> 01:00:19.840
and so Bob's your uncle.

01:00:20.280 --> 01:00:21.940
How much rents are you charging you?

01:00:22.080 --> 01:00:22.300
Nothing.

01:00:22.920 --> 01:00:24.400
He's letting us have it for free?

01:00:24.580 --> 01:00:25.520
Yeah, all for gratis.

01:00:26.040 --> 01:00:28.260
Oh, no, come on, Dale, there's got to be something behind this,

01:00:28.380 --> 01:00:29.920
cos Boycey would scalp you.

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:31.380
if Dandruff had a go in right.

01:00:33.240 --> 01:00:35.560
You're becoming so cynical, Rodney.

01:00:35.660 --> 01:00:37.000
He's just doing a mate a favour, isn't he, eh?

01:00:38.640 --> 01:00:40.360
Wait a minute, you met him in Mario's?

01:00:40.480 --> 01:00:41.240
Yeah, that's right, yeah.

01:00:41.440 --> 01:00:42.320
Grab, Dad, come on, look.

01:00:42.780 --> 01:00:44.420
Clear up all this fishing gear, will you?

01:00:44.440 --> 01:00:45.080
Cos I want to pop out.

01:00:46.180 --> 01:00:47.540
Mario's is a fish restaurant.

01:00:47.700 --> 01:00:48.580
Is it? Yeah, see you later.

01:00:49.080 --> 01:00:50.880
Bit of a coincidence, still, innit?

01:00:50.960 --> 01:00:52.480
You meeting him in a fish restaurant,

01:00:52.620 --> 01:00:54.340
then the next thing we're all going fishing.

01:00:56.500 --> 01:00:58.880
He's like Elliot Bleeding Ness at times, isn't he?

01:01:00.250 --> 01:01:02.530
All right, Rodney, I was going to tell you when we got down here.

01:01:02.670 --> 01:01:04.130
You know, as a sort of surprise, like, you know?

01:01:04.190 --> 01:01:04.350
Oh, yeah.

01:01:04.470 --> 01:01:05.890
Yeah, yeah, as a surprise, yeah.

01:01:06.440 --> 01:01:11.140
Well, this cottage happens to be near one of the finest salmon fishing streams in England.

01:01:11.320 --> 01:01:15.800
Now, Mario has agreed to pay us £10 for every fish that we bring back.

01:01:16.150 --> 01:01:17.670
Now, Boise and I are going to halve it.

01:01:17.730 --> 01:01:18.690
That's a fiver each.

01:01:18.790 --> 01:01:21.690
So let's say that we do, what, 60 fish.

01:01:21.910 --> 01:01:24.310
That'll be 300 sovs in our pocket.

01:01:24.730 --> 01:01:25.890
Now, we split it three ways.

01:01:26.010 --> 01:01:28.770
That means that you and Grandad get £50 each.

01:01:30.640 --> 01:01:33.080
A weekend's fishing and free digs. Now, what do you reckon to that?

01:01:33.440 --> 01:01:34.740
I reckon it's illegal.

01:01:35.800 --> 01:01:38.400
You hurt me sometimes, Rodney. You really do.

01:01:38.460 --> 01:01:41.840
You don't even let me finish before you go jump into your nasty little delusions.

01:01:42.390 --> 01:01:45.910
It's lucky you ain't a judge, Rodney. You dang them before they finish the oath.

01:01:46.810 --> 01:01:49.170
All right, I'm sorry. I just thought...

01:01:49.170 --> 01:01:51.010
I know exactly what you thought.

01:01:53.480 --> 01:01:54.720
So, have we got permission, have we?

01:01:56.190 --> 01:01:59.970
We will have. We see the gamekeeper when we get down there and we pay him.

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:04.460
25 quid what and he gives us a fishing permit no he shows us all in the fence

01:02:06.610 --> 01:02:11.870
it's called business it's called stealing no it ain't rodney listen to your granddad

01:02:11.870 --> 01:02:20.360
it's called poaching and what do we know about that eh dell he can't even poach an egg

01:02:22.280 --> 01:02:28.210
well it'll be a doddle he streams gem-packed with salmon we just put our hooks in and whip them out

01:02:28.210 --> 01:02:29.970
Del, it is illegal, it is...

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:31.300
Moral, it is unethical.

01:02:32.100 --> 01:02:32.540
All right.

01:02:33.080 --> 01:02:36.640
Me and Grandad will go on our own and split the profits between us.

01:02:37.740 --> 01:02:42.040
Now, I didn't say I wouldn't come, did I?

01:02:46.390 --> 01:02:52.170
Poaching, boo-boo-boo, left a sign up on the door.

01:02:52.870 --> 01:02:56.430
Go home poaching, boo-boo-boo, boo-boo-boo.

01:02:56.570 --> 01:02:59.970
You keep on, Rodney, and you're going to get a smack right in the air.

01:03:10.330 --> 01:03:11.370
What's all this about?

01:03:12.260 --> 01:03:14.300
My God, it's the old bilge.

01:03:14.320 --> 01:03:16.600
Someone doubled you up about them salmon.

01:03:17.140 --> 01:03:17.620
Shush.

01:03:18.380 --> 01:03:20.220
Look, just let me do the talking.

01:03:27.880 --> 01:03:28.600
Evening, officer.

01:03:29.240 --> 01:03:29.960
Now, if it's about...

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:34.700
the tax disc i can assure you that the new one is in the post something to do with your road

01:03:34.700 --> 01:03:42.000
fun license sir down for a bit of fishing hour oh no no no nothing like that no why have you got

01:03:42.000 --> 01:03:52.180
three fishing rods tied to your roof rack oh no no because you remember we said we might do a

01:03:52.180 --> 01:03:56.060
little bit of fishing oh yeah that's right yeah yeah i might do you know just a little bit like

01:03:56.060 --> 01:03:56.780
No tootlers.

01:03:57.100 --> 01:03:58.220
No salmon, no.

01:04:03.100 --> 01:04:05.940
You haven't given anyone a lift in the last half hour or so, have you, sir?

01:04:08.120 --> 01:04:09.820
Er, no.

01:04:10.380 --> 01:04:11.700
Look, what is this all about, anyway?

01:04:12.210 --> 01:04:14.930
We just had word that a patient's escaped from the local hospital.

01:04:16.180 --> 01:04:19.210
Escaped? What you got out here? National Health Stallings?

01:04:20.470 --> 01:04:25.090
No ordinary hospital, sir. It's an institute for the criminally insane.

01:04:26.600 --> 01:04:29.200
See, this storm's brought a few power cables down.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:30.960
It helped the entire area.

01:04:31.560 --> 01:04:34.520
It even put the Institute's security system out of action.

01:04:35.480 --> 01:04:39.420
So this patient took his chance and made off across the moors.

01:04:39.580 --> 01:04:42.520
It's out there somewhere now.

01:04:43.640 --> 01:04:45.540
For all I know, he could be watching us.

01:04:48.300 --> 01:04:50.640
What was he in there for, anyway?

01:04:51.290 --> 01:04:54.750
Ten years ago, this very night, he killed a party of weekend fishermen.

01:04:55.550 --> 01:04:59.540
I called him the Axe...

01:05:02.170 --> 01:05:04.890
No, no, I didn't know. I must have been out that night.

01:05:05.770 --> 01:05:07.490
You people, be very careful.

01:05:08.030 --> 01:05:09.490
Don't pick up any hitchhikers.

01:05:09.850 --> 01:05:12.030
Don't stop for anyone, no matter what the circumstances.

01:05:12.450 --> 01:05:16.880
And if you see or hear anything suspicious, phone the police immediately.

01:05:18.320 --> 01:05:20.140
Your lives may depend on it.

01:05:21.440 --> 01:05:23.410
Right, gentlemen, have a nice weekend, won't you?

01:05:23.510 --> 01:05:23.610
Yeah.

01:05:32.520 --> 01:05:34.380
Yeah, well, come on, full ahead both, Rodney.

01:05:34.890 --> 01:05:36.350
Ain't going on, aren't we?

01:05:36.350 --> 01:05:37.290
Yeah, of course we are.

01:05:38.090 --> 01:05:41.550
Bill, there is a crazed axe murderer out there somewhere.

01:05:41.970 --> 01:05:44.870
I know that, Rodders, but you seem to be forgetting

01:05:44.870 --> 01:05:47.110
that we're on a 300 quid earner.

01:05:48.450 --> 01:05:52.030
Don't worry, we'll be locked up safe and sound in Boyce's cottage.

01:05:53.530 --> 01:05:54.950
Anyway, there's three of us.

01:05:56.450 --> 01:05:58.170
Me and you.

01:06:02.330 --> 01:06:04.290
Don't worry, I'll look after you.

01:06:38.730 --> 01:06:41.310
Come on, it's quite granddad.

01:07:01.950 --> 01:07:03.330
You're making me nervous.

01:07:03.870 --> 01:07:07.950
I didn't say I saw someone, did I? Just that I saw something.

01:07:08.490 --> 01:07:10.130
Get them lanterns going, will you, Rodney?

01:07:11.300 --> 01:07:13.100
What's wrong with the lights? There's no electric.

01:07:13.680 --> 01:07:15.000
Someone's been tampering with it.

01:07:15.300 --> 01:07:19.080
No. The storm has blown the power cables over, remember?

01:07:19.360 --> 01:07:20.800
The whole area's blacked out, isn't it?

01:07:21.680 --> 01:07:24.380
I'll see if I can find some candles in this cupboard over here.

01:07:33.550 --> 01:07:33.930
What are you doing?

01:07:34.700 --> 01:07:35.500
Phoning the law.

01:07:35.860 --> 01:07:36.720
You're doing what?

01:07:36.820 --> 01:07:38.360
What are you trying to do to me?

01:07:39.120 --> 01:07:39.520
God!

01:07:40.270 --> 01:07:42.110
Look, we're down here doing a bit of fishing.

01:07:42.680 --> 01:07:46.040
The last thing we need is the local polizia sniffing round our keep nets.

01:07:46.440 --> 01:07:49.720
Look, that cop I said, if we see or hear anything suspicious,

01:07:49.960 --> 01:07:51.280
phone the police immediately.

01:07:51.600 --> 01:07:53.200
Our lives could depend on it.

01:07:53.360 --> 01:07:55.260
All right, then, who have you seen, Hawkeye?

01:07:55.740 --> 01:07:56.660
Oh, I saw...

01:08:00.120 --> 01:08:01.880
A movement in the trees? A movement?

01:08:02.330 --> 01:08:04.250
Of course you've seen a movement in the trees!

01:08:04.820 --> 01:08:06.820
There's a ruddy typhoid blown out there!

